{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' attest/specs/360/spec.md; cat /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5rkeqem1/checks.json; cat /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5rkeqem1/graph.txt; sed -n '1,260p' attavo.toml; rg -n -C 5 \\\"test-bypass|pytest|attavo test|refus|allowed|ATTAVO_FEEDBACK\\\" attest/records/360/build-03.log | tail -n 220; git diff --no-index -- /dev/null /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5rkeqem1/diff.patch >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; rg -n \\\"\"'^(diff --git|'\"\\\\+.*test_|\\\\+.*StatementIntervention|\\\\+.*Intervention|\\\\+.*Literal|\\\\+.*now_iso|\\\\+.*criterion could not check|\\\\+.*exit 2)\\\" /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5rkeqem1/diff.patch | tail -n 300\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' attest/specs/360/spec.md; cat /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5rkeqem1/checks.json; cat /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5rkeqem1/graph.txt; sed -n '1,260p' attavo.toml; rg -n -C 5 \\\"test-bypass|pytest|attavo test|refus|allowed|ATTAVO_FEEDBACK\\\" attest/records/360/build-03.log | tail -n 220; git diff --no-index -- /dev/null /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5rkeqem1/diff.patch >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; rg -n \\\"\"'^(diff --git|'\"\\\\+.*test_|\\\\+.*StatementIntervention|\\\\+.*Intervention|\\\\+.*Literal|\\\\+.*now_iso|\\\\+.*criterion could not check|\\\\+.*exit 2)\\\" /var/folders/k6/kwlls81j5gvf1p1_hbh9mn8m0000gn/T/tmp5rkeqem1/diff.patch | tail -n 300\"","aggregated_output":"## Problem\n\nClass: fix\n\nThe reviews of the 2026-10-14 wave passed with four findings, none blocking, each a few lines. They are one item because each is small and they share a wave.\n\n1. #339's rejection test proves the claim's `at` equals the version's `at`, not that the clock is read once. A call count on `now_iso` for one `plan claims` write proves the stronger claim (the product already reads once; the test is what is missing).\n2. `store.put`'s own stamp, when the caller passes no `at`, has no regression test.\n3. #351's review read the gate as judging criterion kinds before the exit-code contract. The spec's own push found the contract is already judged first: a structural criterion that exits 1 on the tree and 2 on the stub is refused \"criterion could not check (exit 2)\" on main today. The finding needs no logic; its test pins the order.\n4. `attavo/types.py` types an intervention's `class` as `str`; the schema is the enum `amend`, `launch`, `transport`. A TypedDict for an intervention carries it as a `Literal`, and the mirror test reads enums against literals.\n\nThe stub is thin: the four tests, one per finding, in their files; the one that needs logic (4) is red on the stub. The build writes the logic.\n\nRetires: four gaps a second reader found that the first reader's tests did not cover.\n\n## Claims\n\n- attavo/spec.py\n- attavo/types.py\n- attavo/ledger.py\n- tests/test_plan.py\n- tests/test_store.py\n- tests/test_spec_gate.py\n- tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- [structural] the-rejection-tests-exist.sh: the four tests exist, one per finding, in tests/test_plan.py, tests/test_store.py, tests/test_spec_gate.py and tests/test_types_mirror_schemas.py\n- [behavioural] the-intervention-class-type-is-the-schemas-enum.sh: a TypedDict in attavo.types for an intervention types class as the Literal of the schema's enum\n{\n  \"read\": true,\n  \"reason\": null,\n  \"checks\": []\n}\n## the default branch, first-parent, since this item's branch point\n\n(nothing new)\n\n## this branch's own commits since the branch point\n\n4c39d3cb64641af55035d24124fa39836efc50bb attavo executor (claude-code) attavo: type item_acts_and_interventions' interventions as list[StatementIntervention]\n39892e46c041fba06fba7000b481f22766e01e86 attavo driver attavo: build invocation 03 started for item 360\nfcce8c45e51ba7e5ac0c5b5cd2cbe62d9dee451c attavo-records[bot] attavo: approval record for item 360\nec403e9baa08b406a31d4e8dd7b6a4b18fa9521a attavo-records[bot] attavo: spec-gate record for item 360\n2835edee43a5127b2c81f4064c9419ea880fa510 dbean10 Merge branch 'main' into attavo/360-wave-findings\nee0a26242d5a26b1b06beda474291e127f8edd8c attavo-records[bot] attavo: spec-gate record for item 360\nb6ee13b135fd1cc85cac8fc2f539250e01b7d869 dbean10 Update spec.md\na5c67782f9395124c1279c96b420bd59eb6514a6 attavo driver attavo: build record for item 360 (build-02)\n9672d1ec4236c4543bac93b0e61a129ee9ab1b41 attavo driver attavo: build invocation 02 started for item 360\nb6fe84f92cd027c0e60d5e44a59dc0e7257c448a attavo driver attavo: build record for item 360 (build-01)\ne7c8d95c