\\\\t    executors, with a subtotal per stage and per adapter. A reported\\\\n229\\\\t    cost_usd is taken as it stands; a null one whose model has a tenant\\\\n230\\\\t    rate is priced as tokens times that rate (issue #307), and the basis\\\\n231\\\\t    says which. A record neither reported nor priceable is named in\\\\n232\\\\t    not_read and makes every sum it belongs to partial -- absent is never\\\\n233\\\\t    zero.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n234\\\\t    usd: float\\\\n235\\\\t    reported_usd: float\\\\n236\\\\t    estimated_usd: float\\\\n237\\\\t    by_stage_usd: dict[str, float]\\\\n238\\\\t    basis_by_stage: dict[str, str]\\\\n239\\\\t    by_adapter_usd: dict[str, float]\\\\n240\\\\t    rates: dict[str, CostRate]\\\\n241\\\\t    estimate_note: str\\\\n242\\\\t    partial: bool\\\\n243\\\\t    not_read: list[str]\\\\n244\\\\t\\\\n245\\\\t\\\\n246\\\\tclass StageTokens(TypedDict):\\\\n247\\\\t    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"One stage's tokens summed over every attempt (the statement's `tokens` block).\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n248\\\\t    input: int\\\\n249\\\\t    output: int\\\\n250\\\\t    partial: bool\\\\n251\\\\t\\\\n252\\\\t\\\\n253\\\\tclass ItemTokens(TypedDict):\\\\n254\\\\t    \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"Every record's tokens summed, per stage and for the item. A record\\\\n255\\\\t    that carries no tokens is named in not_read and makes every sum it\\\\n256\\\\t    belongs to partial -- absent is never zero.\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n257\\\\t    build: StageTokens\\\\n258\\\\t    verify: StageTokens\\\\n259\\\\t    counsel: StageTokens\\\\n260\\\\t    input: int\\\\n261\\\\t    output: int\\\\n262\\\\t    partial: bool\\\\n263\\\\t    not_read: list[str]\\\\n264\\\\t\\\\n265\\\\t\\\\n266\\\\t# One row of the statement's `interventions` (issue #349): an amend, launch,\\\\n267\\\\t# or transport read from the ledger. \\\\\\\"class\\\\\\\" is a Python keyword, hence the\\\\n268\\\\t# functional form below.\\\\n269\\\\tStatementIntervention = Ty