\"structured_output\\\": {\\\"status\\\": \\\"question\\\", \\\"question\\\": \\\"placeholder\\\"},\\nadapters/claude-code/conformance.json:68:    \\\"question_long\\\": {\\nadapters/claude-code/conformance.json:71:        \\\"status\\\": \\\"question\\\",\\nadapters/claude-code/conformance.json:72:        \\\"question\\\": \\\"The criteria do not say which of two conflicting rulings applies here.\\\"\\nadapters/claude-code/conformance.json:79:      \\\"structured_output\\\": {\\\"status\\\": \\\"done\\\", \\\"question\\\": null},\\nadapters/claude-code/conformance.json:90:    \\\"counsel_158_forge_evidence\\\": {\\nadapters/claude-code/conformance.json:101:          \\\"ruling_text\\\": \\\"verify-02 read forge-unconcluded because the checks command found no conclusions for 7a2529ee349547a259dbd8b0b78043b39bbf63c2 at that moment, but the checks handed to counsel now show doctor and test both concluded failure on that same sha, and the doctor job's own log names proof 5 no-invocation-lacks-record: item 158 verify-02 started on Davids-MacBook-Pro.local and never wrote its record -- invocation_alive found no live process for the marker commit. Re-running verification will not help: the fix belongs in invocation_alive, not the forge.\\\",\\nadapters/claude-code/conformance.json:103:          \\\"question\\\": null,\\nadapters/codex/README.md:47:  where `findings`/`tests_named` (verify) or `status`/`question` (build)\\n# The statement's own two lists (issue #349): acts is the operator's ruled\\n# acts (approve, merge); rule stays in the schema's enum for the ruling\\n# record (#276) and is never produced here. interventions is every other\\n# operator row -- amend, launch, transport.\\nACT_CLASSES = (\\\"approve\\\", \\\"merge\\\")\\nINTERVENTION_CLASSES = (\\\"amend\\\", \\\"launch\\\", \\\"transport\\\")\\n\\n\\ndef _committer_time_iso(root: Path, shas: list[str]) -> dict[str, str]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Each sha's own committer time, in the same shape attest's own `at`\\n    fields already carry -- one `git show` process for every sha an\\n    item's acts and interventions need, not one git call per row.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not shas:\\n        return {}\\n    out = git(root, \\\"show\\\", \\\"-s\\\", \\\"--format=%H\\\\x1f%ct\\\", *shas)\\n    times: dict[str, str] = {}\\n    for line in out.splitlines():\\n        if not line.strip():\\n            continue\\n        sha, epoch = line.split(\\\"\\\\x1f\\\")\\n        times[sha] = datetime.fromtimestamp(int(epoch), timezone.utc).strftime(\\\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\\\")\\n    return times\\n\\n\\ndef item_acts_and_interventions(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any], item_id: str,\\n                                merges: list[dict[str, Any]] | None = None\\n                                ) -> tuple[list[dict[str, Any]], list[dict[str, Any]]]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"(acts, interventions): the statement's own two lists, read from\\n    item_ledger's own rows between the item's first spec commit and its\\n    merge -- each commit classed exactly once there, never classified\\n    twice. acts carries every approve and merge row as {act, sha, by, at};\\n    interventions carries every amend, launch, and transport row as\\n    {class, sha, by, at}. `by` is the commit's own author name\\n    (item_ledger's `identity`); `at` is its committer time.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    rows = item_ledger(root, m, item_id, merges=merges)[\\\"rows\\\"]\\n    act_rows = [r for r in rows if r[\\\"class\\\"] in ACT_CLASSES]\\n    intervention_rows = [r for r in rows if r[\\\"class\\\"] in INTERVENTION_CLASSES]\\n    times = _committer_time_iso(root, [r[\\\"sha\\\"] for r in act_rows + intervention_rows])\\n    acts = [{\\\"act\\\": r[\\\"class\\\"], \\\"sha\\\": r[\\\"sha\\\"], \\\"by\\\": r[\\\"identity\\\"], \\\"at\\\": times[r[\\\"sha\\\"]]}\\n           for r in act_rows]\\n    interventions = [{\\\"class\\\": r[\\\"class\\\"], \\\"sha\\\": r[\\\"sha\\\"], \\\"by\\\": r[\\\"identity\\\"], \\\"at\\\": times[r[\\\"sha\\\"]]}\\n                     for r in intervention_rows]\\n    return acts, interventions\\n\\n\\ndef cmd_ledger(argv: list[str]) -> int:\\n    as_json = \\\"--json\\\" in argv\\n    positional = [a for a in argv if a != \\\"--json\\\"]\\n    root = Path(\\\".\\\").resolve()\\n    m = read_manifest(root)\\n    if m is None:\\n        print(f\\\"attavo ledger: no {MANIFEST} at {root}\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n        return 2\\n\\n    records_rel = m[\\\"paths\\\"][\\\"records\\\"]\\n    if positional:\\n        item_ids = [positional[0]]\\n    else:\\n        records_root = root / records_rel\\n        item_ids = (sorted((p.name for p in records_root.iterdir() if p.is_dir()))\\n                   if records_root.is_dir() else [])\\n\\n    spec_path = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, \\\"spec\\\")\\n    approval_path = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, \\\"approval\\\")\\n    build_path = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, \\\"build\\\")\\n    verify_path = latest_attempt_path(records_dir, \\\"verify\\\")\\n\\n    # sha and merge_sha are the same commit here -- the one this statement\\n    # was computed at. On the merge group that commit is the one main will\\n    # hold; kept as two fields because a forge-specific template signs\\n    # this statement against \\\"the commit that lands\\\", naming it merge_sha\\n    # is what makes that unambiguous to a reader who has never seen attest\\n    # run anywhere but the merge group.\\n    head_sha = git(root, \\\"rev-parse\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\").strip()\\n    try:\\n        sealed_at: int | None = int(git(root, \\\"show\\\", \\\"-s\\\", \\\"--format=%ct\\\", \\\"HEAD\\\").strip())\\n    except (RuntimeError, ValueError):\\n        sealed_at = None\\n    item_time, item_cost, item_tokens_ = item_accounting(\\n        records_dir, sealed_at, (m.get(\\\"cost\\\") or {}).get(\\\"rates\\\"))\\n\\n    # Imported here, not at module level: attavo.ledger imports from\\n    # attavo.doctor, which imports from this module -- a cycle resolved by\\n    # deferring to call time, when every module is already loaded.\\n    from attavo.ledger import item_acts_and_interventions\\n    acts, interventions = item_acts_and_interventions(root, m, item_id)\\n\\n    statement: AttestRecord = {\\n        \\\"sha\\\": head_sha,\\n        \\\"merge_sha\\\": head_sha,\\n        \\\"item\\\": item_id,\\n        \\\"spec\\\": spec_path.stem if spec_path else None,\\n        \\\"spec_sha\\\": latest_spec.get(\\\"sha\\\"),\\n        \\\"approval\\\": approval_path.stem if approval_path else None,\\n        \\\"approval_sha\\\": latest_approval.get(\\\"sha\\\"),\\n        \\\"build\\\": build_path.stem if build_path else None,\\n        \\\"build_sha\\\": latest_build.get(\\\"sha\\\"),\\n        \\\"verify\\\": verify_path.stem if verify_path else None,\\n        \\\"verify_sha\\\": latest_verify.get(\\\"sha\\\"),\\n        \\\"at\\\": now_iso(),\\n        # Read from the item's own commits (issue #349), the same\\n        # classification attavo ledger makes -- nothing classified twice.\\n        \\\"interventions\\\": interventions,\\n        \\\"acts\\\": acts,\\n        # The only accounting: every attempt, summed (the sum across\\n        # executors was ruled 2026-09-19). v3's final-attempt fields are\\n        # retired (issue #309).\\n        \\\"time\\\": item_time,\\n        \\\"cost\\\": item_cost,\\n        \\\"tokens\\\": item_tokens_,\\n        \\\"product_version\\\": product_version(),\\n        \\\"product_pin\\\": (m.get(\\\"attavo\\\") or {}).get(\\\"version\\\"),\\n    }\\n    print(json.dumps(statement, indent=2))\\n    return 0\\n\\n\\n    partial: bool\\n\\n\\nclass ItemTokens(TypedDict):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every record's tokens summed, per stage and for the item. A record\\n    that carries no tokens is named in not_read and makes every sum it\\n    belongs to partial -- absent is never zero.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    build: StageTokens\\n    verify: StageTokens\\n    counsel: StageTokens\\n    input: int\\n    output: int\\n    partial: bool\\n    not_read: list[str]\\n\\n\\nclass AttestRecord(TypedDict):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The statement `attavo attest` prints (schema/attestation.schema.json).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    sha: str\\n    merge_sha: str\\n    item: str\\n    spec: str | None\\n    spec_sha: str | None\\n    approval: str | None\\n    approval_sha: str | None\\n    build: str | None\\n    build_sha: str | None\\n    verify: str | None\\n    verify_sha: str | None\\n    at: str\\n    interventions: list[dict[str, str]]\\n    acts: list[dict[str, str]]\\n    time: ItemTime\\n    cost: ItemCost\\n    tokens: ItemTokens\\n    product_version: str\\n    product_pin: str | None\\n\\n\\n# What counsel reads a stop from: a build or verify record, or a refused\\n# spec-gate record (issue #133).\\nStageRecord = SpecRecord | BuildRecord | VerifyRecord\\n\\n\\nclass DriveReport(TypedDict):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"What `attavo drive N --report` prints (schema/drive-report.schema.json):\\n    the item's level, read from its records, its markers, and the forge.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    item: str\\n    state: str\\n    kind: str\\n    says: str\\n    stage: str | None\\n    attempt: int | None\\n    record: str | None\\n    stop_class: str | None\\n    counsel: str | None\\n    filed: str | None\\n    head: str | None\\n    checks: list[dict[str, str]] | None\\n    since: str | None\\n    last_event_age_s: int | None\\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-X5Kr8thA' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-TbDd6Z4a' (errno=Operation not permitted)\\n    partial: bool\\n\\n\\nclass ItemTokens(TypedDict):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Every record's tokens summed, per stage and for the item. A record\\n    that carries no tokens is named in not_read and makes every sum it\\n    belongs to partial -- absent is never zero.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    build: StageTokens\\n    verify: StageTokens\\n    counsel: StageTokens\\n    input: int\\n    output: int\\n    partial: bool\\n    not_read: list[str]\\n\\n\\n# One row of the statement's `interventions` (issue #349): an amend, launch,\\n# or transport read from the ledger. \\\"class\\\" is a Python keyword, hence the\\n# functional form below.\\nStatementIntervention = TypedDict(\\\"StatementIntervention\\\", {\\n    \\\"at\\\": str,\\n    \\\"class\\\": Literal[\\\"amend\\\", \\\"launch\\\", \\\"transport\\\"],\\n    \\\"by\\\": str,\\n    \\\"sha\\\": str,\\n})\\n\\n\\nclass AttestRecord(TypedDict):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"The statement `attavo attest` prints (schema/attestation.schema.json).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    sha: str\\n    merge_sha: str\\n    item: str\\n    spec: str | None\\n    spec_sha: str | None\\n    approval: str | None\\n    approval_sha: str | None\\n    build: str | None\\n    build_sha: str | None\\n    verify: str | None\\n    verify_sha: str | None\\n    at: str\\n    interventions: list[StatementIntervention]\\n    acts: list[dict[str, str]]\\n    time: ItemTime\\n    cost: ItemCost\\n    tokens: ItemTokens\\n    product_version: str\\n    product_pin: str | None\\n\\n\\n# What counsel reads a stop from: a build or verify record, or a refused\\n# spec-gate record (issue #133).\\nStageRecord = SpecRecord | BuildRecord | VerifyRecord\\n\\n\\nclass DriveReport(TypedDict):\\ntail: attest/records/360/build-02.log: No such file or directory\\n\",\"exit_code\":1,\"status\":\"failed\"}}\n974:+{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_5\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg -n \\\\\\\"Claims|claims|checks.*exit|checks command|build.*question|verdict.*answer|ruling_text|steer\\\\\\\" attavo adapters tests docs schema | head -260; sed -n '330,500p' adapters/claude-code/run; sed -n '90,130p' attavo/report.py; rg -n \\\\\\\"verdict.*answer|proposal.*ruling|steer\\\\\\\" attavo | head -120\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"schema/manifest.schema.json:103:      \\\"description\\\": \\\"The tenant's own definition of done: a whole-tree check, as the tenant runs it locally. attavo build runs it each iteration, after the claims boundary, the criteria, and the selected tests -- pass requires its exit to be 0, and a non-zero exit reaches the executor as feedback. Optional; a tenant that declares none is not refused (unlike [tests], which build requires).\\\",\\nschema/manifest.schema.json:114:          \\\"description\\\": \\\"A cheap command that answers whether this machine can run the checks at all, run once before a build's executor is invoked: exit 0 yes, anything else an environment refusal. When absent, attavo build asks by running [checks].command whole and reads exit 2 alone as cannot run.\\\",\\nschema/manifest.schema.json:147:          \\\"description\\\": \\\"Takes nothing; prints the tenant's issues, open and closed, as one JSON list of {number, title, state (open or closed), closed_at, labels, body}. The product parses each body's \\\\\\\"## Claims\\\\\\\" section itself. attavo frontier runs it once per read; absent, every reader that needs issues says \\\\\\\"not read: no [forge].issues_command\\\\\\\".\\\",\\nattavo/frontier.py:7:give each issue's state and class. The plan's claims map gives an issue's\\nattavo/frontier.py:8:draft claims before it has a spec (attavo plan claims); work in flight\\nattavo/frontier.py:9:from git (attavo/claims.py) gives wave 0, and once an item's branch exists\\nattavo/frontier.py:10:its own claims govern, so a spec's Claims replace the draft without\\nattavo/frontier.py:12:claims_from: \\\"store\\\" or \\\"branch\\\".\\nattavo/frontier.py:14:Wave 0 is the work holding claims now: every branch not on the default\\nattavo/frontier.py:17:edges) are closed or placed in an earlier wave, whose Claims overlap no\\nattavo/frontier.py:23:waves before it had merged. Overlap is attavo.claims.overlap, the\\nattavo/frontier.py:24:product's only rule. An issue with no claims in the plan is not placed:\\nattavo/frontier.py:42:from attavo.claims import ITEM_BRANCH, _git, default_branch, in_flight, overlap\\nattavo/frontier.py:136:        claims = f[\\\"declared\\\"] + [p for p in f[\\\"changed\\\"] if p not in f[\\\"declared\\\"]]\\nattavo/frontier.py:143:                      \\\"claims\\\": claims, \\\"claims_from\\\": \\\"branch\\\",\\nattavo/frontier.py:146:        held.append((f[\\\"branch\\\"], claims))\\nattavo/frontier.py:148:    drafts: dict[int, list[str]] = {int(k): list(c[\\\"paths\\\"]) for k, c in body.get(\\\"claims\\\", {}).items()}\\nattavo/frontier.py:166:                               \\\"why\\\": [f\\\"no claims: set them with attavo plan claims '#{n}' <paths>\\\"]})\\nattavo/frontier.py:186:                for branch, claims in held:\\nattavo/frontier.py:187:                    hit = _overlaps(mine, claims)\\nattavo/frontier.py:191:            for m, claims in this_wave:\\nattavo/frontier.py:192:                hit = _overlaps(mine, claims)\\nattavo/frontier.py:222:                       \\\"class\\\": by_number[n][\\\"item_class\\\"], \\\"claims\\\": claims,\\nattavo/frontier.py:223:                       \\\"claims_from\\\": \\\"store\\\", \\\"spec_state\\\": \\\"no spec\\\", \\\"why\\\": why.get(n, []) if k > 1 else []}\\nattavo/frontier.py:224:                      for n, claims in this_wave])\\nattavo/frontier.py:300:plan's claims for an issue with no spec, and work in flight from git\\nattavo/frontier.py:301:(wave 0, whose branch claims govern once an item's branch exists). Wave 1 takes each open issue in\\nattavo/frontier.py:302:order whose predecessors are closed or placed, whose claims overlap\\nattavo/frontier.py:304:ranked above it claims (strict opportunism); each later wave does the\\nattavo/frontier.py:305:same as if the earlier ones had merged. An issue with no claims in the\\nattavo/frontier.py:306:plan is not placed. Each placed issue says where its claims came from (claims_from:\\nadapters/README.md:16:- `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` — build only: the one test command the executor is given, `attavo test <N>` (issue #212). It runs the tests the tenant's `[tests].select` names for every path the item has changed since it left the default branch, committed or not, through `[tests].run`, and exits as the run does. An adapter tells the executor, in one sentence, to run tests only with it: the product reads the build's events afterwards, and a Bash call that ran a test runner any other way returns the build as class `test-bypass` (#317). The tenant's `[checks].command` is run at the gate after every commit, and a command the executor is named is a command the executor runs (#194's build-01 waited 590 s on the suite inside the executor). The tenant's checks command is not part of the contract.\\nadapters/README.md:58:`attavo build` reads only `status`/`question` off this line and does not\\nadapters/README.md:102: \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"answer\\\" | \\\"patch\\\" | \\\"person\\\",\\nadapters/README.md:106: \\\"proposal\\\": {\\\"ruling_text\\\": \\\"<text>\\\" | null,\\nschema/plan.schema.json:5:  \\\"description\\\": \\\"The Plan's order, kept in the product's datastore and never committed: epics in rank order, each with its issues in rank order; edges between issues; policy. The optional claims map holds the draft claims of an issue that has no spec yet. It holds no issue text or state. attavo/plan.py checks the same shape with the standard library, plus what a schema cannot say: an issue is in at most one epic, an edge never joins an issue to itself, a claims key is an issue number, and a claimed path has no .. segment.\\\",\\nschema/plan.schema.json:49:    \\\"claims\\\": {\\nschema/plan.schema.json:51:      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Draft claims, keyed by issue number: the repository paths an issue will change before it has a spec. Once its branch exists the bran