ts/test_cli_registry.py:6:Run: python3 -m pytest tests -q\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:44:Run: python3 -m pytest tests/test_executor_conformance.py -q\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:52:import pytest\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:176:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:185:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:192:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:198:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:217:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:245:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:252:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:259:    command = \"python3 /product/bin/attavo test 7\"\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:271:    assert \"attavo test\" not in without[\"instruction\"]\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:274:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:326:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:339:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:353:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:365:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:387:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/tests/test_executor_conformance.py:417:@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"adapters/claude-code/run -- see README.md (this directory) for the four\nconfiguration keys, and ../README.md for the shared adapter contract.\n\nA live `claude` invocation is not exercised by the test suite (judgment\nis measured, not tested); its argument construction is checked by\nATTAVO_ADAPTER_DRY_RUN=1, which prints the `claude` command line as a\nJSON array instead of running it, its response handling is checked by\nATTAVO_ADAPTER_RESPONSE_FILE, which reads a canned final report object\nfrom a file instead of invoking `claude`, and (issue #26) its\n`--output-format stream-json --verbose` mapping -- the event stream\nthis adapter maps to ATTAVO_EVENTS, and the terminal \"result\" line it\nreads the report object from -- is checked by ATTAVO_ADAPTER_STREAM_FILE,\nwhich feeds a recorded transcript instead.\n\nThe whole result is printed to stdout before this adapter's own final\nline, so build-NN.log carries it as the transcript -- a halt otherwise\ncannot be explained after the fact. is_error or an absent\nstructured_output exit 1 on either stage; a build status \"question\"\nwhose question is missing or under MIN_QUESTION_CHARS characters also\nexits 1 (build records the attempt as failed) rather than a halt\nsomeone must rule on.\n\nATTAVO_STAGE=verify branches to a different objective, schema, and\nreport shape (issue #46): the instruction states the verify objective\n(see verify_instruction) instead of the build one, --json-schema is\nVERIFY_SCHEMA instead of STATUS_SCHEMA, and the final line carries\nfindings and tests_named instead of status and question.\n\nIssue #78: the boundary is the tool's own sandbox, not a curated\nallowed_tools list judged per sub-command -- confirmed live (recorded on\nthe issue, 2026-09-10) against `claude 2.1.268`: `--settings` carrying\n`{\"sandbox\": {\"enabled\": true, \"allowUnsandboxedCommands\": false}}` under\n`-p` refuses a write outside the working directory (\"operation not\npermitted\") and, with `network.allowedDomains: []`, refuses an outbound\nconnection (\"deny network-outbound ...\"), both before `--allowedTools`\nis ever consulted. build's `--settings` therefore enables the sandbox and\nforbids the unsandboxed fallback; verify's additionally sets\n`filesystem.denyWrite` on the working directory itself (confirmed live:\n`denyWrite` takes a list of paths, not a bare boolean -- `true` alone did\nnot stop a write inside the directory). `--allowedTools` shrinks to the\ntool names each stage may use at all -- `Read,Edit,Write,Bash` for build,\n`Read,Bash` for verify -- since Edit and Write are not Bash and the\nsandbox does not govern them. `allowed_tools` is retired as a manifest\nkey: a config that still declares it is refused by name rather than\nsilently accepted.\n\nIssue #88 (class A: a report is not a question). `--json-schema`\nconstrains the tool's structured_output to \"done\"/\"question\", but\nnothing stops \"question\" from carrying a status report rather than an\nactual question -- confirmed against tenant zero's own corpus, five\nspecimens with no \"?\" anywhere in the text. A \"question\" whose text\nclears MIN_QUESTION_CHARS but contains no \"?\" is a report, not a\nquestion: this adapter re-invokes the executor once, appending\nREINSTRUCTION to the same instruction, before ever reporting a halt to\na person. A second report in a row still halts (someone must look), but\nits report line carries \"class\": \"non-question\" and both raw results\nreached stdout above it -- an extra field bin/attavo's own record schema\ndoes not know about and never has to: it reads \"status\"/\"question\" off\nthis line exactly as before, so a \"question\" halt still halts. Read via\nATTAVO_ADAPTER_RESPONSE_FILE, a JSON array is a queue -- one canned\nresult per invocation this adapter makes, its last element repeating\nonce exhausted -- while a single object still repeats for every call,\nunchanged.\n\nIssue #88 (class B: work that outlives the invocation). Confirmed live,\nthis machine, `claude 2.1.269`: with both \"Agent\" and \"Task\" allowed, a\nprompt asking for a subagent produced `subagent_stats.spawned: 1`, `\"Agent\"`\nalone in `--disallowedTools` (Task is not a distinct tool in this build)\nbrought it back to 0 -- the tool's own reply named \"Workflow\" as the\nother path to background work, so both are named here. `--allowedTools`\nis an allow-list a background spawn does not consult (tenant zero's\nspecimen: `--allowedTools` without \"Agent\" or \"Workflow\" in it at all did\nnot stop three of them), so this adapter also disallows them by name on\nboth stages and, after the run, refuses by name -- exit 1, not a\nhalt -- any response whose subagent_stats.spawned is not zero, with the\ncounts in the message. A tool that reports no subagent_stats at all\n(spawned absent or 0) is unaffected; this is a refusal on evidence, not a\nguess from the flag.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# the helper beside adapters/, imported without leaving a __pycache__ there\nsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent))\nfrom executor_env import executor_env  # noqa: E402\n\nSTATUS_SCHEMA = {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": False,\n    \"required\": [\"status\", \"question\"],\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"status\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"done\", \"question\"]},\n        \"question\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n    },\n}\n\n# The verify objective (issue #46): a verifier reports findings, not a\n# commit. additionalProperties: False means the tool cannot hand back a\n# structured_output shaped like STATUS_SCHEMA's status/question by\n# accident -- an absent findings key is what cmd_verify treats as\n# failed, not a lenient default here.\nVERIFY_SCHEMA = {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": False,\n    \"required\": [\"findings\", \"tests_named\"],\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"findings\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n                \"required\": [\"title\", \"specimen\", \"retires\", \"rejection_test\", \"severity\"],\n                \"properties\": {\n                    \"title\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                    \"specimen\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                    \"retires\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                    \"rejection_test\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                    \"severity\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                },\n            },\n        },\n        \"tests_named\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1}},\n    },\n}\n\n# The counsel objective (issue #100): a stop is read inside the product\n# first, before a person. additionalProperties: False for the same reason\n# as VERIFY_SCHEMA's own -- the tool cannot hand back a differently-shaped\n# structured_output by accident.\nCOUNSEL_SCHEMA = {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": False,\n    \"required\": [\"class\", \"verdict\", \"citations\", \"proposal\"],\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"class\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n        \"verdict\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"answer\", \"patch\", \"person\"]},\n        \"citations\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"additionalProperties\": False,\n                \"required\": [\"kind\", \"path\", \"symbol\", \"ruling_id\"],\n                \"properties\": {\n                    \"kind\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"instruction\", \"mechanism\", \"guard\"]},\n                    \"path\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n                    \"symbol\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n                    \"ruling_id\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n                },\n            },\n        },\n        \"proposal\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"additionalProperties\": False,\n            \"required\": [\"ruling_text\", \"patch\", \"question\", \"issue\"],\n            \"properties\": {\n                \"ruling_text\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n                \"patch\": {\n                    \"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"],\n                    \"additionalProperties\": False,\n                    \"required\": [\"file\", \"symbol\", \"rejection_test\", \"diff\"],\n                    \"properties\": {\n                        \"file\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                        \"symbol\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                        \"rejection_test\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                        \"diff\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                    },\n                },\n                \"question\": {\"type\": [\"string\", \"null\"]},\n                # issue #175: the fourth proposal shape, for a \"patch\" or\n                # \"person\" verdict whose remedy is better filed as an item\n                # than shipped as a diff or asked as a bare question.\n                \"issue\": {\n                    \"type\": [\"object\", \"null\"],\n                    \"additionalProperties\": False,\n                    \"required\": [\"title\", \"body\"],\n                    \"properties\": {\n                        \"title\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                        \"body\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 1},\n                    },\n                },\n            },\n        },\n    },\n}\n\n\ndef read_text(path_env: str) -> str:\n    path = os.environ.get(path_env)\n    if not path:\n        return \"\"\n    p = Path(path)\n    return p.read_text() if p.is_file() else \"\"\n\n\ndef describe_file(path: str, text: str, diff_like: bool) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Path, byte count, line count, and (for a diff) files touched --\n    named in the instruction instead of inlining the file's own text, so\n    the instruction stays a small fixed size whatever the file's size\n    (issue #86: a 27,367-line deletion diff inlined whole exceeded a\n    judge's input ceiling -- codex's, on the specimen that surfaced it).\n    Files touched counts unified-diff file headers (`diff --git a/...\n    b/...`), the shape `git diff` produces.\"\"\"\n    size = Path(path).stat().st_size\n    lines = text.count(\"\\n\") + (1 if text and not text.endswith(\"\\n\") else 0)\n    if not diff_like:\n        return f\"`{path}` ({size} bytes, {lines} lines)\"\n    files = sum(1 for l in text.splitlines() if l.startswith(\"diff --git \"))\n    return f\"`{path}` ({size} bytes, {lines} lines, {files} files touched)\"\n\n\ndef spec_sections() -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"The spec's Problem, Claims, and Criteria sections verbatim -- what\n    both build and verify need to see, in the shape the spec contract\n    (not this adapter) already gives them.\"\"\"\n    spec_dir = Path(os.environ[\"ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR\"])\n    lines = (spec_dir / \"spec.md\").read_text().splitlines()\n    idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(\"## \")]\n    headings = {lines[i].strip(): i for i in idx}\n    bounds = sorted(idx) + [len(lines)]\n\n    def section(heading: str) -> str:\n        start = headings[heading]\n        end = bounds[bounds.index(start) + 1] if start in bounds else len(lines)\n        return \"\\n\".join(lines[start:end]).strip()\n\n    return [section(\"## Problem\"), section(\"## Claims\"), section(\"## Criteria\")]\n\n\ndef stub_note() -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"None when ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR carries no stub/; else the sentence\n    naming what a stub is (issue #90, closed by #93). The stub is\n    evidence -- a criterion it satisfies trivially is weak -- but twice\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/doctor.py:577:    a records transport: more than one parent, or a path outside\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/doctor.py:596:        outside = [p for p in paths if not (p.startswith(prefix) and \"/\" in p[len(prefix):])]\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/doctor.py:597:        if outside:\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/doctor.py:598:            bad.append(f\"{sha[:12]} touches {outside[0]}, outside its item's records\")\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/doctor.py:1056:    not \"everything outside paths.records\", so a commit that lands\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/testtool.py:301:def runner_calls_outside_the_tool(events: list[dict[str, Any]],\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/testtool.py:553:executor); they run outside one and in CI. When ATTAVO_EVENTS is set, one\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:25:               \"foreign-commit\", \"test-bypass\")\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:28:# #317 a fifth, test-bypass, retried with the steer \"run tests only with\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:32:RETRYABLE_CLASSES = (\"died\", \"hung\", \"transient\", \"returned\", \"test-bypass\")\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:97:        foreign-commit -> foreign-commit/tenant; test-bypass ->\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:98:        test-bypass/executor (a Bash call ran a test runner other than\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/stops.py:123:        if refusal_kin